---
import DocsLayout from '@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { CodeBlock, Callout, DocsTable } from '@/molecules/DocComponents/DocComponents';
---

<DocsLayout breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Docs', href: '/docs' }, { label: 'Architecture', href: '/docs/architecture' }, { label: 'Agents', href: '/docs/architecture/agents' }, { label: 'LORE (Documentation)' }]}>
  <h1>LORE  -  Documentation Agent</h1>

  <p>
    LORE is the technical writer. It activates after every successful merge and never
    interrupts active development. LORE generates Architecture Decision Records, updates
    <code>CHANGELOG.md</code>, and maintains project history. <strong>Disabled by default</strong>  - 
    enable in <code>registry.json</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Trigger</h2>

  <p>
    LORE is triggered by the <code>ticket_merged</code> event emitted by VESSEL. This event
    contains the ticket ID, PR number, and repository. LORE never runs during active
    development  -  only post-merge.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock lang="bash">{`# LORE reads the event
openflows-harness event listen ticket_merged

# Output: { ticketId, prNumber, repo, mergedAt }`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>Artifacts Produced</h2>

  <DocsTable headers={['Artifact', 'Location', 'Description']} rows={[
    ['ADR', '<code>docs/adr/NNNN-title.md</code>', 'Architecture Decision Record for significant changes'],
    ['CHANGELOG.md', 'Repository root', 'User-visible changes with PR references'],
    ['README updates', 'As needed', 'Public API changes, new configuration options'],
    ['Workflow docs', '<code>docs/workflows/</code>', 'Updated process documentation'],
  ]} />

  <h2>ADR Template</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="markdown">{`# docs/adr/0042-rate-limiting.md

---
title: Rate Limiting Middleware
date: 2026-07-20
status: Accepted
ticket: ISSUE-42
pr: #123
---

## Context
The PocketFlow executor needed resilient retries for transient failures (network blips, rate limits).
Previous implementation had no retry logic, causing cascading failures.

## Decision
Add exponential backoff with jitter to Node::run(). Persist retry count in SharedStore
so restarts resume from correct count. Emit node_retry / node_failed events for observability.

## Consequences
- Positive: Transient failures self-heal; operators see retry events in TUI
- Negative: Slightly increased latency for failing nodes; additional state in SharedStore
- Neutral: Max retries default 3; configurable via registry.json

## Alternatives Considered
- Circuit breaker pattern (too complex for v1)
- Fixed retry delay (doesn't handle throttling well)
- No retries (status quo  -  operator burden)
`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>CHANGELOG.md Format</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="markdown">{`## [Unreleased]

### Added
- Rate limiting middleware with exponential backoff (ISSUE-42, #123)

### Changed
- NodeState now includes retry_count field

### Fixed
- Workspace teardown now waits for heartbeat daemon to stop`}</CodeBlock>

  <h2>Configuration</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="json">{{
  "agents": {
    "lore": {
      "provider": "anthropic",
      "model": "claude-haiku-4-20250514",
      "coder_module": "aider",
      "active": false,
      "instances": 1
    }
  }
}}</CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="tip" title="Enable LORE">
    Set <code>"lore": { "active": true }</code> in <code>registry.json</code>. LORE is lightweight
    and runs on <code>claude-haiku</code>, making it cost-effective.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Harness Integration</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="bash">{`# Write documentation
openflows-harness doc write --adr 0042 --content "..."

# Commit to default branch via GitHub MCP
openflows-harness git commit --branch main --message "docs: ADR 0042 rate limiting"

# LORE does NOT open PRs  -  commits directly to main`}</CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="info" title="Direct commit to main">
    LORE commits documentation directly to the default branch via GitHub MCP. It does not
    open a separate PR unless the registry policy is configured to require one.
  </Callout>

  <h2>Read-Only Access</h2>

  <p>
    LORE has <strong>read-only access to application code</strong>. It cannot modify
    source files, only documentation files. This prevents accidental code changes
    by the documentation agent.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>